{"name":"Birdhouse Brown","hex":"#6c483a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"birdhouse","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small house or nest box for birds.","An aviary."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/birdhouse"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nest box","blocks":[{"text":"A nest box, also spelled nestbox, is a man-made enclosure provided for animals to nest in. Nest boxes are most frequently utilized for birds, in which case they are also called birdhouses or a birdbox/bird box, but some mammals such as bats may also use them. Placing nestboxes or roosting boxes may also be used to help maintain populations of particular species in an area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Bluebird_house_%28480393025%29.jpg/330px-Bluebird_house_%28480393025%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nest_box","wikidata":"Q744112"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown","wikidata":"Q47071"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Bat_box_in_Jamaica_Bay_Wildlife_Refuge_%2841119%29.jpg/500px-Bat_box_in_Jamaica_Bay_Wildlife_Refuge_%2841119%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org